 "conclusions": {
  "algebra": "Exact on the 62-element basis (hence on all of the realization by multilinearity): closure, even bracket, graded antisymmetry, super-Jacobi on all 62^3 ordered triples, vanishing Killing form str(ad_x ad_y) on all 62^2 ordered pairs, strict [SW (17)] block rule on all ordered pairs, ad_Delta eigenvalues, [g,g] = g, trivial centre, even part = two commuting 15-dimensional ideals with nondegenerate Killing forms.  All pass: True.",
  "master_equation_su2_complete_on_basis": {
   "arity1": true,
   "arity2": true,
   "arity3": true
  },
  "master_equation_su3_complete_on_basis": {
   "arity1": true,
   "arity2": true,
   "arity3": true
  },
  "every_gauge_algebra": "Every term of the arity 0, 1, 2, 3 components is a g-independent coefficient times a connected tree tensor built from ([-,-],-) and the inverse pairing, with k <= 5 legs (structural bound: S has <= 4 g-valued fields and its antifield-dependent terms <= 3, S^(1) <= 3, S^(2) = 2, and a bracket removes two; the computed pieces have at most 4, 4, 3, 2 field factors at arities 0, 1, 2, 3).  In any g the k-leg tree tensors span a quotient of the multilinear free Lie algebra on k-1 letters, of dimension (k-2)! (1, 1, 2, 6 for k = 2, 3, 4, 5).  In su(2) the ranks are 1, 1, 2, 6, so evaluation on su(2) is injective and S_k-equivariant on trees with k <= 5 legs; an S_k-equivariant left inverse commutes with total derivatives, so a component that is a total derivative for su(2) is a total derivative for every g with a nondegenerate invariant pairing.  With the complete su(2) basis checks this proves the arity 1, 2, 3 components for every such g; arity 0 (classical master equation, <= 5 legs) follows the same way from the su(2) check; arity 4 reduces to {S^(2),S^(2)} = 0 identically and arity >= 5 has no terms."
 }
